## outside_a_frame_method
error[Z0401]: `fixture_rows` reads the frame around it and stands inside a frame method such as `add` or `aggregate`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | fixture_rows()
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^ no frame here
  |
  = help: write it inside a definition, as in `wages.add(y = fixture_rows(...))`

## outside_through_a_function
error[Z0401]: `fixture_rows` reads the frame around it and stands inside a frame method such as `add` or `aggregate`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:5
  |
3 |     fixture_rows()
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^ no frame here
  |
  = help: write it inside a definition, as in `wages.add(y = fixture_rows(...))`

## a_project_function_marking_a_parameter
error[Z0101]: nothing is called `enclosing` here
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:23
  |
2 | fn rows(data: Frame = enclosing) -> Int {
  |                       ^^^^^^^^^ not a binding
  |
  = help: the enclosing frame belongs to a built-in's file (Engine and Project Specification, section 9.1); a project function takes the frame as an argument, `data: Frame`, and is called as a method on it

## the_mark_on_a_helper
the Zeff source of data::bad_fixture does not build:
  error[Z0323]: the enclosing frame belongs to the built-in's own `fn` line
   --> data/functions/bad_fixture.zeff:13:24
     |
  13 | fn _rows(data: Frame = enclosing) -> Int {
     |                        ^^^^^^^^^ `= enclosing`
     |
     = help: a helper takes the frame as an argument: `_rows(data: Frame, ...)`, called with the frame `bad_fixture` was given

## not_the_first_parameter
the Zeff source of data::bad_fixture does not build:
  error[Z0323]: the enclosing frame is the first parameter
   --> data/functions/bad_fixture.zeff:8:40
    |
  8 | fn bad_fixture(var: Var, data: Frame = enclosing) -> Int {
    |                                        ^^^^^^^^^ `= enclosing`
    |
    = help: write `data: Frame = enclosing` first, before the arguments a call gives

## not_a_frame
the Zeff source of data::bad_fixture does not build:
  error[Z0323]: the enclosing frame is typed `Frame`
   --> data/functions/bad_fixture.zeff:7:31
    |
  7 | fn bad_fixture(data: Frame? = enclosing) -> Int {
    |                               ^^^^^^^^^ `= enclosing`
    |
    = help: write `data: Frame = enclosing`; the frame method the call stands in supplies a frame, never `NA`

## a_page_entry_for_the_enclosing_frame
the Zeff source of data::bad_fixture does not build:
  error[Z0323]: the help of `bad_fixture` describes `data`, the enclosing frame, which a call never gives
   --> data/functions/bad_fixture.zeff:3:1
    |
  3 | /// data: The frame around the call.
    | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ no entry for the enclosing frame
    |
    = help: the page lists the arguments of the usage line; say in the description that the function stands inside a frame method
